## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to implement defense-in-depth for cross-tenant OAuth security and a robust rollback.

## Key Concepts
- OAuth2/OIDC, Managed Identities, Conditional Access, PIM
- Private Endpoints, VNet integration, RBAC scoping
- Defender for Cloud, UEBA, alerting
- Secrets rotation and rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal token validation sketch for a Node.js API
const express = require('express');
const jwt = require('jsonwebtoken');
function authorize(requiredScope) {
  return (req, res, next) => {
    const token = req.headers.authorization?.split(' ')[1];
    if (!token) return res.sendStatus(401);
    const decoded = jwt.decode(token, { complete: true });
    if (!decoded || !decoded.payload.scp?.includes(requiredScope)) return res.sendStatus(403);
    next();
  };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test token leakage incidents and validate rollback effectiveness?
- What telemetry and dashboards would you provision to detect anomaly token usage?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of Azure Policy and how to implement guardrails that cover new and existing resources, plus rollout and rollback planning.

## Key Concepts
- Azure Policy and Initiatives
- Deny vs DeployIfNotExists vs AuditIfNotExists
- Storage Account security controls (public access, HTTPS, encryption)
- Tag-based governance and rollout strategy

## Code Example
```javascript
{
  "policyRule": {
    "if": {
      "allOf": [
        { "field": "type", "equals": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts" },
        { "field": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts/publicAccess", "notEquals": "None" },
        { "field": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts.enableHttpsTrafficOnly", "notEquals": true },
        { "field": "tags.env", "exists": false }
      ]
    },
    "then": { "effect": "deny" }
  },
  "parameters": {}
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle existing storage accounts that violate these rules during rollout?
- What metrics and alerts would you configure to monitor policy compliance over time?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design end-to-end, production-grade guardrails for cross-tenant deployments in Azure, focusing on identity, secret management, policy gates, canaries, and UEBA automation.

## Key Concepts
- Workload identities and Just-In-Time access
- Azure Key Vault with per-service managed identities
- Azure Policy gates to block secrets in config
- Azure Lighthouse for cross-tenant governance
- Canary deployments with feature flags and automatic rollback
- UEBA via Azure Sentinel with automated playbooks

## Code Example
```json
{
  "policyRule": {
    "if": {
      "field": "type",
      "in": ["Microsoft.Web/sites", "Microsoft.AzureFunctionsJobHost"]
    },
    "then": {
      "effect": "auditIfNotExists",
      "details": {
        "type": "Microsoft.KeyVault/vaults/secrets"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the policy in a non-prod environment?
- What metrics trigger the automated rollback and how are they evaluated?
